{"uid":"33e2a66f97eb93ef","name":"[ELITEA-1790] test_max_five_skills_attach_limit[chromium]","fullName":"tests.ui.skills.test_agent_max_five_skills_limit.TestAgentMaxFiveSkillsLimit#test_max_five_skills_attach_limit","historyId":"3029cd192094733963a43ac337c03a7a","time":{"start":1791977805608,"stop":1791977952868,"duration":147260},"description":"Create 6 Skills + an Agent, attach 5 of the Skills one at a time,\n        verify the add-skill control disables at 5/5 with a tooltip (rather\n        than a literal 6th-click rejection), and verify persistence via a\n        full page reload.\n\n        Steps (AFS test-specs/skills/lp1_max-5-skills-per-agent_ELITEA-1790.md):\n        1. Create 6 distinct Skills via the UI, under run-unique names — the\n           first 5 are the attach set, the 6th is never attached and backs\n           Step 9's \"no 6th attach\" assertions. The case's own Test Data\n           table instructs the test to create 6, so the precondition is\n           owned by the test rather than borrowed from pre-existing project\n           data.\n        1b. Confirm all 6 created Skills read back from the project.\n        2. Create an Agent.\n        3. Skills section starts at 0/5, add-skill control enabled.\n        4-8. Attach Skills 1-5 one at a time; counter increments \"N/5 skills\n           added.\" and a card renders after each attach.\n        9. Add-skill control becomes disabled the instant 5/5 is reached,\n           with an accessible tooltip — a 6th skill cannot be attached.\n        10. Confirm persistence via a full page reload (attach is\n           auto-saved via API; no explicit agent-level Save is available).\n        ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Create 6 Skills + an Agent, attach 5 of the Skills one at a time,<br />\nverify the add-skill control disables at 5/5 with a tooltip (rather<br />\nthan a literal 6th-click rejection), and verify persistence via a<br />\nfull page reload.</p>\n<pre><code>    Steps (AFS test-specs/skills/lp1_max-5-skills-per-agent_ELITEA-1790.md):\n    1. Create 6 distinct Skills via the UI, under run-unique names — the\n       first 5 are the attach set, the 6th is never attached and backs\n       Step 9's &quot;no 6th attach&quot; assertions. The case's own Test Data\n       table instructs the test to create 6, so the precondition is\n       owned by the test rather than borrowed from pre-existing project\n       data.\n    1b. Confirm all 6 created Skills read back from the project.\n    2. Create an Agent.\n    3. Skills section starts at 0/5, add-skill control enabled.\n    4-8. Attach Skills 1-5 one at a time; counter increments &quot;N/5 skills\n       added.&quot; and a card renders after each attach.\n    9. Add-skill control becomes disabled the instant 5/5 is reached,\n       with an accessible tooltip — a 6th skill cannot be attached.\n    10. Confirm persistence via a full page reload (attach is\n       auto-saved via API; no explicit agent-level Save is available).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"failed","statusMessage":"AssertionError: add-skill button should be disabled once 5/5 skills are attached\nassert False\n +  where False = is_add_skill_button_disabled(timeout=10000)\n +    where is_add_skill_button_disabled = <pages.agent_detail_page.AgentDetailPage object at 0x7f9d48a568d0>.is_add_skill_button_disabled","statusTrace":"tests/ui/skills/test_agent_max_five_skills_limit.py:273: in test_max_five_skills_attach_limit\n    assert detail_page.is_add_skill_button_disabled(\nE   AssertionError: add-skill button should be disabled once 5/5 skills are attached\nE   assert False\nE    +  where False = is_add_skill_button_disabled(timeout=10000)\nE    +    where is_add_skill_button_disabled = <pages.agent_detail_page.AgentDetailPage object at 0x7f9d48a568d0>.is_add_skill_button_disabled","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1791977